  "worked_solution": "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\u0394x,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+j\u0394x$, and  $\u0394x=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=2$ and $b=5,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\n\u0394x=\\frac{5-2}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})\u0394x & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+j\u0394x)\u0394x \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(2+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{3}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2(2+\\frac{3j}{n})-4) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\,\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{6j}{n}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
